      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. it's a decent start but it's a bit vague. the software is flagging it as \"low quality\" because the scientific name count is super low. \n\ncan you beef up the summary by incorporating more specific scientific names for the groups mentioned (like the primates, birds, and the understory plants)? just make sure it still reads like a coherent report on the ecosystem health like i said before. i don't want it to look like a shopping list, but we need that name count to go up so it passes the internal check.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
